{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to the previous sweep comment, finding 1.\n\nThe `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:177` docstring hit is **already fixed** by `25a4-1ab3-3558-4cd4`'s pending commit `3a1388cde72` (\"Drop deleted alias name from test docstring\"), which rewrites that sentence to say \"the legacy alias table\" instead of naming `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`. Once 25a4 lands, that survivor is gone.\n\nThe AC1 problem is unchanged and still blocking. The remaining survivors after 25a4 lands:\n\n- the **19 `_ALIASES\\b` over-matches** on unrelated live identifiers (`_ARCH_ALIASES`, `_HIDDEN_ALIASES`, `_REMOVED_SIMPLE_CLI_ALIASES`, `_EDIT_FLAG_ALIASES`, `_DEPRECATED_PROVIDER_ALIASES`) — this is the load-bearing defect;\n- `_map_legacy_env` in `tests/fixtures/cloud_adf_corpus/bodies_00.json` and `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/table.json`, captured ticket prose that must not be edited.\n\nAlso worth noting for sequencing: 25a4 is the only other story touching this file, and it touches nothing else in cb2b's scope, so re-measuring cb2b's citations after 25a4 and ed5a land will not move anything beyond that one line."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793421431595733069,"uuid":"8b9406a5-f1c8-44f5-96bf-ac4744694032"}